WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
San Francisco, 1945.

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.910
Representatives of 50 countries
draft a charter for a new world body.

3
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:13.730
Today it has 193 member states:
almost every state on Earth.

4
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.850
One body holds primary responsibility
for peace and security:

5
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.030
the Security Council.

6
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.030
Fifteen seats, five permanent.

7
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.830
On decisions of substance, any
one of the five can block it.

8
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.170
So with five countries able
to block its decisions,

9
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.070
can the UN still keep the world stable?

10
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:34.670
In this mission, you'll
weigh the UN's tools,

11
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.970
from sanctions to force, on real cases.

12
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:42.550
Then you'll see what happens when
powerful states act outside the UN.

13
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.150
Your mission: evaluate whether the
UN can still keep the world stable.
